cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in scientific work, please cite it as below."
title: "AutoDisloc: dislocation density of hcp titanium alloys (Ti-6Al-4V, CP-Ti) from X-ray line profile analysis (mWH, mWA and Wilkens whole-profile fitting)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Memu
    given-names: Fırat
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3485-7040"
    affiliation: "TOBB University of Economics and Technology"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fmemu/AutoDisloc"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.xxxxxxx"                             # TODO: concept DOI after the first Zenodo release
abstract: >-
  AutoDisloc computes the dislocation density, the Burgers-vector population and the
  dislocation arrangement parameter of hcp alpha/alpha' titanium alloys (e.g. Ti-6Al-4V,
  CP-Ti) from laboratory X-ray
  diffraction patterns. The main result comes from fitting the Wilkens dislocation model,
  a log-normal size distribution and the Dragomir-Ungar hexagonal contrast factors directly
  to the measured profiles (CMWP-type whole-profile analysis); the modified Williamson-Hall
  analysis gives the Burgers-vector population, and a Voigt-based modified Warren-Averbach
  analysis is reported for comparison. Desktop program for macOS and Windows
  (Turkish/English), command-line interface, publication-ready figures and tables, a user
  manual and a whitepaper.
keywords:
  - X-ray diffraction
  - line profile analysis
  - dislocation density
  - modified Williamson-Hall
  - modified Warren-Averbach
  - Wilkens model
  - contrast factor
  - Ti-6Al-4V
  - titanium alloys
  - additive manufacturing
references:
